   F: Does the function w, with w(x) = 1 for x >= 0 and w(x) = -1 for x < 0, have a limit at 0?
   B: No. |w(x)| = 1 for every x, so w is bounded, but its left-hand limit at 0 is -1 and its right-hand limit is 1. By Proposition 2.2 the two-sided limit at 0 does not exist (Misconception 2).
